WEBVTT

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:05.230
<i>Now reach your hand out and take hold,</i>

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.600
<i>of the one and only me.</i>

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.400
<i>Sing my praises out loud,</i>

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.530
Hey, what on earth are those things?!

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.660
<i>about how special I am.</i>

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.660
What are you?

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.550
<i>Don't be afraid, come close.</i>

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.490
What's going on here?!

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.490
This way!

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:26.100
<i>Love me, though I'm no one.</i>

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:38.890
<i>I don't want to accept that 
I'm the same as others.</i>

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:34.840
Get down!

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:46.060
<i>If I pretend not to see, and 
conveniently close my eyes,</i>

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.060
What are you doing?

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:49.570
What has to be done.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.220
Hey, what are those?!

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.500
I'll explain later!

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:30.290
For now, just run!

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.390
I don't think we should get involved.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.000
I heard from my friends.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.100
They call that man the fighter.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.140
The fighter?

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:56.110
That's clearly more than just a normal fight.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:56.780
It's useless!

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.390
She can't see them.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:00.700
She can't...

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.240
Huh, what do you?

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.410
There's no end to them.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:06.960
Hey?!

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.000
Shikishima-kun?!

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.210
Mizuguchi-san!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.560
That woman's fine!

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.710
Right now, worry about yourself!

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.250
Hurry up. If they catch you, it's over.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.560
The fighter, Satake Shogo!

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.230
I see he's out there getting 
into trouble as usual.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.860
Thanks for the great pieces again today!

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:41.970
<b>Cancel</b>

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.740
<b>One file has been selected.</b>

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.740
<b>Select</b>

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.050
That guy with him was...

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:48.180
That same guy who caused a fuss at 
the entrance ceremony, right?

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.360
What on earth are those two up to?

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.940
I want to know!

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.900
You should just accept it and enjoy it more.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:26.140
I'm sure you're feeling guilty about 
abandoning your classmate to get here,

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:27.630
but as I said,

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:28.780
she'll be fine.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.950
Do you have proof of that? 
Why I should believe you?!

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.560
You're a stubborn one.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.230
She hasn't noticed.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:46.890
So those things won't attack her.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:50.560
Hasn't noticed... what?

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:55.670
What? Something you and 
I have already realized.

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:57.770
You know what I mean, right?

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.280
You really don't?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.360
But in that case, why did that 
musician only half awaken you?

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:16.250
What are you saying you've noticed?

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.580
Well...

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:20.340
You know...

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.040
You won't talk about 
yourself either, will you?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.740
I can't trust you.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:29.640
You're...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.460
You're the first one like me I've found.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:35.940
Like you?

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:40.770
Ah, jeez!

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.740
Shogo, you suck at explaining!

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.370
I was just about to tell him 
about it from the beginning.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:50.620
You can't do it, so I'll explain for you.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.630
Hello! I'm Aria!

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:56.210
Ritsu, please! Save μ!

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.990
What's this pipsqueak?

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:04.380
That tickles! That tickles! 
And who's a pipsqueak here?!

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.670
This isn't time for that, you know!

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:11.390
You were able to hear my voice, right?

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.130
Your voice?

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.520
Stop μ! Save μ!

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.610
That was you?!

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:20.820
Yes.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:24.980
Something awful has happened to μ.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.040
So, please! Save μ!

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:31.160
Please, please, I really need your help.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:35.450
Or in this case, help μ?

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.040
Help what?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.290
Don't ask me.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.540
Um... I still don't follow 
what you're saying.

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.360
Your explanation is too vague!

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.180
That's not my fault!

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:52.510
My power, body, memory and 
everything else have floated off.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:56.100
It's still better than 
your rough explanation!

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.210
What was that?!

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.980
What?!

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.190
Come with me!

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.190
He's gone.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.230
<i>Shikishima-kun?</i>

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:27.430
Mizuguchi-san, how have, uh...

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.840
How did it go?

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.470
<i>Huh? Nothing important's happened.</i>

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.080
<i>I just got back from the opening ceremonies.</i>

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:35.020
I see.

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:36.970
<i>Honestly, what's wrong with you?</i>

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:40.490
<i>You're acting rather weird 
today, Shikishima-kun.</i>

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.990
Mizuguchi-san...

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.660
<i>What is it?</i>

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.280
<i>Shikishima-kun?</i>

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.900
No, it's nothing.

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:54.120
<i>Maybe you're getting worn out from reading 
all those complicated books all the time?</i>

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.560
You think so?

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.120
<i>Oh, right. You were mentioned by the gossiper.</i>

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:01.870
<i>I'll send it to you.</i>

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:04.040
<i>Well, see you tomorrow at school!</i>

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.660
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.220
<b>You all know about the school 
troublemaker, Satake Shogo?
If you know anything, send it over!</b>

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:15.340
This is from earlier?!

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.810
<b>Is he strong in a fight?

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.310
<b>Is he strong in a fight?

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:22.810
<b>Kishimai's mad dog appears lol
Narukonne</b>

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.310
<b>Shogo-chan's the one 
getting attacked lolololol

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:27.760
So there is a discrepancy 
in everyone's cognition.

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:29.440
Mass hysteria?

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.680
That, or...

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.820
No, that wouldn't explain it.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.740
The most likely answer is...

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.700
<b>Man, Shogo-chan'll attack anyone he sees 
wearing a Kishimai uniform, won't he?

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:44.420
that I'm the one who's mad.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:51.080
I hope Ritsu's okay.

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:53.480
It would be nice if he stays safe.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.530
Yeah. We need to do something 
before those guys capture him.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:01.470
Ah!

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.740
This is you and Ritsu!

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.100
You're being recorded in secret?!

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.610
What, what? Someone's obsessed with you?

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.270
Is it a stalker?

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:12.200
I know! I know!

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:16.460
Shogo, you've made enemies
 in a lot of places, huh?

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:19.490
<b>Does anyone know anything about the commotion at the 
entrance ceremony hall today? Intel please!! 
Narukonne</b>

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:20.960
What's the matter?

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:23.130
We might be able to use this.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:24.360
What do you mean?

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:25.830
When we were in the auditorium...

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.800
There were others who reacted 
like Shikishima Ritsu.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:32.990
There should be those in that 
group who managed to run

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:35.110
and escape from the Digiheads for now.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:37.840
You're right!

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:40.010
Let's go gather up the others!

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.060
The more heads we have, the better.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:50.940
We're okay.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.210
It looks like they all went somewhere else.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.300
Cheer up!

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.540
Tomoe Kotaro-sama is on your side!

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:01.020
Why did everyone...

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:03.880
Is there something wrong with us now?

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.410
That's not it!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:10.020
My mind has been feeling 
funny since that commotion.

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:13.880
Like I'm me, but not me.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:17.180
I-I'm not feeling funny at all!

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:19.850
It's my duty to rescue those in trouble.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.760
I don't have time to be acting funny.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.890
You'll be fine, too! 
I'm sure everyone just got sick!

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.220
I saw on TV...

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:33.620
There's some kind of nasty virus in 
ants or spiders that explodes outward.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:37.440
Sorry!

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:39.910
I wasn't trying to scare you or anything.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:50.210
Answer, answer...

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:54.170
Dammit.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:58.320
Nothing from Takatsu or Yumita...

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.090
Did they already...

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:03.240
Ritsu? You home?

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:05.300
Oh, I'm home.

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:12.760
Do you know about our store's app?

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:17.390
You can earn great savings 
just by downloading it.

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:19.030
Please give it a try.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:22.740
Wha? This... is human?

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:25.470
Do you know about our store's app?

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:29.620
You can earn great savings 
just by downloading it.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.580
Please give it a try.{I think this one is muffled and should be skipped?}

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:44.970
Welcome home. How were 
your entrance ceremonies?

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.380
Welcome home. How were 
your entrance ceremonies?

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.330
How were your entrance ceremonies?

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:59.990
<b>Anxiety, Irritation, and Other Such 
Negative Emotions Spread to Others</b>

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:10.390
You're home, Mifue-chan?

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:15.290
<b>Butter roasted mackerel</b>

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.290
<b>Lamb confit</b>

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:18.410
Welcome home, Mifue-chan.

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:21.150
What would you like for dinner tonight?

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:23.930
Butter roasted mackerel? Lamb confit?

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.320
You can ask for anything.

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:29.000
I'll make whatever you'd like, Mifue-chan.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:30.140
Stop it!

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:32.700
Take care while you're out.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:35.100
Come home before it gets too late.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.660
Oh, sorry.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:54.890
What's with him?

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.470
Hey, let's go.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.190
Think.

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:19.480
Think.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.400
Think.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:23.600
Think.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:24.360
Think.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:26.110
Think.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.450
Think.

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:35.870
<b>Takatsu</b>

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:35.870
<b>Calling</b>

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:35.870
<b>End             Answer</b>

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.740
Takatsu, you're okay?!

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:39.450
<i>Are you okay?</i>

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:42.660
<i>What have you been doing since you 
ran out of the entrance ceremonies?</i>

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:47.000
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.120
<i>Hm? What is it?</i>

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.050
At the entrance ceremonies today...

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:54.350
Back then, did you see anything strange?

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:57.500
<i>Huh? Is your head okay?</i>

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.480
<i>Where are you right now, Ritsu?</i>

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.130
<i>Let's meet up and talk.</i>

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:06.100
<i>Come on, man!</i>

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.390
All right.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:11.160
Then let's meet at the traffic circle in 
front of the station in one hour.

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:15.540
Suzuna, hurry!

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:19.580
What is that?

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:25.050
I don't know, but there's 
one thing I'm sure of!

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:28.460
The guys back at school 
aren't the only crazy ones.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:33.310
Where to, ma'am?

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:37.660
Tokyo.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:47.650
Man, Ritsu sure is late!

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:51.120
He's the one who said an "in an hour," too.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:55.420
Maybe he forgot since he's been 
spacing out a lot here lately.

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:02.010
Hello, you alive?

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:05.210
<i>I've been thinking about a 
lot of things since then.</i>

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:06.110
Hm?

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:10.830
If there were a bacterial infection 
causing some kind of pandemic,

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:13.910
and if this city were the 
source of the outbreak,

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:16.810
then it should have spread 
further outside the city by now.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:19.220
But from my investigation,

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:22.580
there hasn't been a single report of 
any such incidents on any news sites.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.770
No images have been recorded 
on smartphone cameras, either.

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:29.150
<i>There's a large discrepancy 
between what I saw</i>

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.930
<i>and what other people have perceived.</i>

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:35.210
Hey! None of this is very interesting.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.740
Where are you?!

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.930
So I thought there was some kind of

00:15:39.930 --> 00:15:43.160
irregularity with my own 
vision and hearing,

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:47.210
causing visual and auditory hallucinations.

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:50.670
At least until I noticed this...

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:07.800
<i>My heartbeat resonates through the sky,</i>

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:07.800
I knew it.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:12.920
<i>through endless, repeating days,</i>

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:13.050
μ's song was always playing when 
people like you would attack me.

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:17.260
Plus, this sight is unmistakably 
not an illusion.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:20.230
<i>as I carry my hidden wounds.</i>

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.410
I'm not the one who has gone mad.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.830
I'm not crazy!

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.800
It would seem there's someone 
your feelings haven't reached.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:32.890
Why?

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:35.720
What am I doing wrong?

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:41.930
I just want to make 
everyone happy. That's all.

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:47.400
We, the Ostinato Musicians, 
will show them the way, so don't worry.

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:51.820
Now, please sing for them, μ.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:58.160
<i>Hey, let's stare into each other's eyes 
and race through the night sky.</i>

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:05.400
<i>Don't cry. I'll fly again in your eyes.</i>

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:09.380
<i>What's going on here?</i>

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.400
Them, too?!

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:21.310
<i>There's a bunny playing amongst the comets,</i>

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:27.100
<i>In this dazzlingly dark universe</i>

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:30.190
Ritsu, you're late!

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:32.600
<i>It's mysterious, and mysterious 
that it's mysterious.</i>

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:33.020
You really kept us waiting!

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:35.530
So, what did you want?

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:38.650
<i>I found your voice here again,</i>

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:47.000
<i>and aging stars burst in supernovas,</i>

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:50.790
<i>giving birth.</i>

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:50.790
Damn, they're appearing again!

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:56.620
<i>In this nebulous sadness, 
no matter how scared you are,</i>

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:52.710
Suzuna, hurry!

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:02.470
<i>I'll always hold you tight.</i>

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.340
<i>Now departing.</i>

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:08.360
<i>When the gentle breeze blows 
throw the cracks of our cosmos,</i>

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:16.010
<i>I'll accept all your desires,</i>

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:13.800
I knew it, these ones with the staticky heads

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:17.740
seem different from the pointy-headed
 ones that attacked us earlier.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:20.670
<i>In the orbit of our souls.</i>

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:30.140
What are you so dissatisfied with?

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:38.570
<i>Don't turn around, your home 
is here, isn't it? Right?</i>

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.340
We've been having a fun 
time together, haven't we?

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:34.500
Right, Ritsu?

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:41.090
I finally found you.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:45.930
<i>You don't have to strong. You can be pitiful.</i>

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:43.600
Rogue.

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:44.220
Eliminate!

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.410
Shogo! Get them!

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:51.270
<i>Just keep believing, in my eyes.</i>

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:59.430
So hot-blooded.

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:09.180
Takatsu, Yumita...

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:12.250
You all right, Shikishima Ritsu?

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.450
Hey! You!

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:17.360
I won't keep you here anymore.

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:18.590
Shogo?!

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:20.930
But if you feel like talking...

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:25.390
We'll be in the music prep room 
inside the old school building.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:28.890
Was it okay to let him go like that?

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:30.350
Who knows?

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.400
But nothing others say

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:39.800
can help anyone accept it.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:43.450
Until they confirm it with their own eyes,

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.530
they have no way to understand

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.930
the circumstances they've been thrown into.

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:56.390
<i>Next Stop, Okitama. Okitama.</i>

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:59.040
<i>This is the final stop for this train.</i>

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:03.110
<i>Please be sure to take your belongings 
and be careful as you leave.</i>

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:06.180
I thought the last stop was much farther out?

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:12.020
They're telling us to get 
off here? What's going on?

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.210
Right, Suzuna?

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:14.480
Hm?

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:16.270
Hey!

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:18.410
We haven't made it to Tokyo!

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:36.710
If this is a pandemic, I'm not 
the one suffering from it.

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:39.190
Then, what's...

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:45.840
What is this?!

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:11.260
I'm sorry.

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:13.710
I haven't created anything past this point yet.

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:18.790
Right now, I can't create any 
farther regions for Mobius.

00:21:19.100 --> 00:21:21.710
What do you mean? What are you saying?!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:24.760
I can create anything else you'd like, though.

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:26.470
What would you like?

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:28.640
A new family?

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:31.310
Friends? Or...

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:38.520
Oh, right...

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:43.230
I need to search for my mother.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:47.050
<i>I finally understand.</i>

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:50.950
<i>Neither myself, Takatsu, 
nor the others were mad.</i>

00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:56.000
<i>This world is mad!</i>

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:31.080
Chirp, chirp.

00:23:27.230 --> 00:23:34.680
<b>Episode 3
Why do we live? The further we pursue
 the meaning of life, the more confused we become.</b>

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:30.800
Oh, no! I've confused the president!

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:32.380
Why do we live?

00:23:32.380 --> 00:23:36.310
The further we pursue the meaning of life,
 the more confused we become.

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:39.310
Are you really confused?

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:39.980
I am.

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:41.020
Chirp, chip.
